From 5081037c60bc8976dbfa2225d0fb785b58e12242 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 18:44:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/15] ppc: G4/G5 port - SDL2/GLFW platform layer and legacy
 fixed-function GL renderer

Replaces upstream's SDL3 + GLES/Vulkan-only stack with a Platform interface
(SDL2/SDL3/GLFW) and a RenderBackend interface with a legacy fixed-function
OpenGL implementation, so ImTube runs on G4 and G5 Power Macs under Mac OS X
10.4-10.6 alongside every platform upstream supports: NPOT texture padding
for pre-GL-2.0 GPUs, a packed BGRA upload path, per-machine default stream
resolution, and macOS OpenGL.framework vs Mesa selection.

