+On macOS the build links the system `OpenGL.framework`, because that is the
+library behind the Cocoa video driver SDL2/SDL3/GLFW use there (also on
+10.4/10.5 PowerPC). It deliberately does not go through CMake's
+`find_package(OpenGL)`: with MacPorts' cmake (frameworks searched last) and
+the `mesa` port installed, that returns Mesa's X11 `libGL.dylib`, which never
+sees the Cocoa context. The symptom is a black window and
+`glGetString called without a rendering context` on stderr; ImTube now
+refuses to start in that state and says so. To run under XQuartz with Mesa
+instead, build with `-DIMTUBE_MACOS_GL=x11` and start with
+`SDL_VIDEODRIVER=x11`. The `[platform]` line on stderr shows the driver in
+use, e.g. `SDL 2.32.10 (cocoa)`.
